A||||3||billfredmike24||Door adjustment?||||1||
Z||000000||billfredmike24||09-01-2001||01:59 AM||||My drivers side door has about a 2" chunk out of it from the previous owner hitting the bottom of the sail panel with the door.  How do i adjust the door so it won't happen again.<BR>Thanks Mike<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_10.jpg"> <BR>yeah the wheels are ugly, and the stickers, that'll change||||reg||1
Z||000001||maryjane||09-01-2001||03:25 AM||||Sounds like the hinge pins and/or the bushings may be worn out. Replacing them may bring it back where it should be. There is an article (neat little trick!) in The Ogre's cave about putting a spacer on the bottom of the hinge to help position the door and keep the hinge from wearing against itself. Other than that it is a trial and error deal when it comes to adjusting the hinges. It's a pita especially if you are by yourself. It's been too long ago for me to remember the details, seems like I had to remove an inside panel on my '84 to adjust one of them.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||09-01-2001||02:20 PM||||Hey Mike!<BR>Perhaps the door skin has crept up?<BR>Is the top of the skin even or below the dew wipe?<BR>If it is over the dew wipe, the skin needs to be repositioned down...<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/page1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||09-01-2001||04:32 PM||||sounds like spent hinge pins.<P>Door skin creep up? can't see how unless hardware is missing. The 2 screws under the trim pretty much lock it in place.||||reg||1
